# Public-repo .gitattributes — line-ending pins ONLY.
#
# The private repo's .gitattributes is deliberately NOT shipped by
# scripts/publish-engine-oss.sh: it git-LFS-tracks binaries (*.png, *.glb, *.hdr, *.ttf, …), and the
# public CI does not fetch LFS, so shipping it would make every test read pointer text instead of a
# binary. Public binaries are stored inline instead — simpler, and no LFS quota.
#
# But dropping the whole file also dropped the EOL normalisation, and that half matters on its own.
# Without it the public repo falls back to `* text=auto`, so a Windows checkout (autocrlf=true is
# the GitHub runner default) gets CRLF while our generators emit \n — and every
# generated-vs-committed comparison fails with two strings that look IDENTICAL in the diff.
#
# That is not hypothetical: it is exactly how the private Windows CI leg failed on its first run
# (the generated .codex/config.toml read as permanently stale), and it is how the PUBLIC Windows leg
# failed on ITS first run — engine/tests/tools/toolCatalogSync.test.ts, comparing the generated MCP
# tool catalog against docs/debug-tools-mcp.md.
#
# So: the EOL pins ship, the LFS filters do not. Keep this file free of `filter=lfs` lines.

# Force LF for source files
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.mts text eol=lf
*.cts text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.swift text eol=lf
*.java text eol=lf
*.kt text eol=lf
*.kts text eol=lf
*.podspec text eol=lf
*.gradle text eol=lf
*.rb text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.plist text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Small binaries (kept in-tree, not LFS)
*.ico binary
